; Two load-time verdicts on `:multiple-of`, and the difference between them
; is the point.
;
; `:multiple-of 0` is an **error**. The check divides by this value, and the
; alternative reading — "every number is a multiple of 0" — is not one anyone
; wants a schema to state.
;
; `:multiple-of -8` is an **error** too, and for a second reason on top of
; that one: it divides exactly what `8` divides, so allowing it buys nothing,
; and JSON Schema 2020-12 requires `multipleOf` to be strictly positive — so a
; host that accepted it exported a schema no validator will compile. Both
; signs share one arm and one message.
;
; `:multiple-of 0.25` is a **warning**, not an error. It is meaningful and it
; works; it is only approximate, because divisibility is exact in integer
; space and a fractional divisor falls back to a floating-point remainder
; against a tolerance. Rejecting it would forbid a working schema, so the
; author is told instead. The bound is still stored and still checked.
;
; No document body: both diagnostics come from the manifest phase, and adding
; a usage would only pile `unknown_form` on top once the errored plugin is
; dropped from the schema.
(plugin :name gfx :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name zero-divisor
    :underlying number
    :numeric (numeric-bounds :multiple-of 0))

  (value-kind :name negative-divisor
    :underlying number
    :numeric (numeric-bounds :multiple-of -8))

  (value-kind :name quarter
    :underlying number
    :numeric (numeric-bounds :multiple-of 0.25)))
